I agree.

I should point out that a fu'ivla creator should think of "jiebroda test"=
=20
for fu'ivla morphology if "consonant glide" is allowed for cmavo. If both=
=20
cmavo and fu'ivla may include "consonant glide", "jiebroda" is not a=20
fu'ivla (or zi'evla) but two words "jie broda". In order to make it fu'ivla=
=20
form, we should modify it, for example, to "djiebroda" or "ji'ezbroda".

Actually, vlatai of jbofi'e says "jie" is not a lojban word, "jiebroda",=20
"djiebroda" and "ji'ezbroda" are fu'ivla (stage-4), while camxes says "jie"=
=20
is cmavo, "jiebroda" is two words, "djiebroda" is not a lojban word, and=20
"ji'ezbroda" is fu'ivla.

Whether cmavo with "consonant glide" is allowed or not is very important=20
for defining Lojban phonology. I, who have been believed that "consonant=20
glide" is basically a kind of non-lojban sound, I have not been much=20
careful in listening and speaking "je". If "jie" is allowed as cmavo, I=20
should change my attitude, and be careful whether the pronunciation is "je"=
=20
or "jie". Please, BPFK-members, make clear the decision on this matter.=20

--=20
